From c5037ebd839b2ec7ecf38a78aa8861cb14b1dd78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:29:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] android: Nintendo services settings on the Network screen

Settings > Network now has a "Nintendo services" part like the desktop's
Configure > General > Network: "Use a custom server", the server address,
"Share my games with the server" and "Connect as a Nintendo Zone hotspot".
The address and game sharing are greyed out while the custom server is
off. They are the same config.ini settings ([WebService]) the native side
already reads, so no more editing config.ini by hand on a phone. The room
settings (Web API URL, token) follow under their own "Network / Room"
header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
---
 .../tangelo/features/settings/SettingKeys.kt  |  4 ++
 .../features/settings/model/BooleanSetting.kt | 13 +++++-
 .../features/settings/model/StringSetting.kt  |  3 +-
 .../settings/ui/SettingsFragmentPresenter.kt  | 45 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml       | 12 +++++
 5 files changed, 75 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

